@startuml
title SysMon - Managing User Access Sequence Diagram

participant "SysMon Frontend" as Frontend
participant "SysMon Authentication System" as Auth
participant "SysMon Backend" as Backend

note over Frontend
  Admin (Tier 1) opens the Users panel and selects Manage Access.
  At any step the admin may cancel or close the panel:
  no request is sent and no changes are introduced.
end note

== Select a user ==
Frontend -> Auth : GET /v1/users?page=1&pageSize=20\nAuthorization: Bearer token
Auth --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{items, page, pageSize, total}
Frontend -> Auth : GET /v1/users/{userId}\nAuthorization: Bearer token

alt Token missing, invalid or expired
  Auth --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
else Caller is not a Tier 1 admin
  Auth --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
else User does not exist
  Auth --> Frontend : 404 Not Found\n{code, message}
else User found
  Auth --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{userId, username, tier, status, permissions}
end

note over Frontend, Auth
  The same 401 and 403 answers apply to every
  request of this diagram.
end note

alt Admin tier of the user is modified
  Frontend -> Auth : PATCH /v1/users/{userId}\nAuthorization: Bearer token\n{tier}

  alt Token missing, invalid or expired
    Auth --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
  else Caller is not a Tier 1 admin
    Auth --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
  else User does not exist
    Auth --> Frontend : 404 Not Found\n{code, message}
  else Data invalid (tier is not 1, 2 or 3)
    Auth --> Frontend : 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{code, field, message}
  else Last Tier 1 admin would lose Tier 1
    Auth --> Frontend : 409 Conflict\n{code, message}
  else All checks passed
    Auth -> Auth : Modify admin tier of the chosen user
    Auth --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{userId, username, tier, status, permissions}
  end
else Permissions are modified
  Frontend -> Backend : GET /v1/compute-groups, /v1/containers\nor /v1/storage-groups\nAuthorization: Bearer token
  Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{items, page, pageSize, total}

  Frontend -> Auth : PATCH /v1/users/{userId}/permissions\nAuthorization: Bearer token\n{changes}
  Auth -> Backend : GET /v1/containers/{objectId}\n(or compute-groups, storage-groups)
  Backend --> Auth : 200 OK or 404 Not Found

  alt Token missing, invalid or expired
    Auth --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
  else Caller is not a Tier 1 admin
    Auth --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
  else User or object does not exist
    Auth --> Frontend : 404 Not Found\n{code, message}
  else Data invalid (unknown object type or permission)
    Auth --> Frontend : 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{code, field, message}
  else All checks passed
    Auth -> Auth : Modify permissions of the chosen user
    Auth --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{userId, permissions}
  end
end

@enduml
